# Modern right-click orders on the shoplifter-1 replay (chapter 7, ch04), played with --modern.
# The player's ships there: the liner (initial 0, takes no orders), the rescue transport
# (initial 1), the flagship (initial 5) and an escort (initial 6) whose destination the level locks.
# Select friendly (action 8) cycles through them; after each, a right-click on empty space near
# the top right of the play area: only an orderable ship moves, the others are only targeted.
300 key 8
330 rclick 560 120
600 key 8
630 rclick 560 120
900 key 8
930 rclick 560 120
# A right-click on the centre of the play area, where the flagship always is: follow it.
1200 rclick 368 240
# Zoom to show all (action 26), then a right-click where a Gaitori cruiser (initial 8) is drawn:
# attack it. The click lands on the right ship at the new zoom.
1450 key 26
1500 rclick-initial 8
# What a level's "target" action does: the transport ordered back to the liner, its first
# destination. The scripted order replaces the Modern one.
1800 script-target 1 0
